T*
T*
(1. Introduction) Tj
T*
(The selected application is a PHP/MySQL-based car booking portal that enables) Tj
T*
(customers to browse vehicles, make reservations, and allows administrators to manage) Tj
T*
(the fleet. The legacy codebase relied on ad-hoc scripts with minimal security) Tj
T*
(controls, resulting in multiple critical vulnerabilities. This project modernised) Tj
T*
(the security posture, remediated the highest-risk flaws, and introduced Google) Tj
T*
(OpenID Connect login to strengthen authentication.) Tj
T*
T*
T*
(2. Assessment Methodology) Tj
T*
(The team adopted a repeatable process that combined manual inspection with automated) Tj
T*
(assistance:) Tj
T*
T*
T*
(1. **Source code review:** Analysed PHP, HTML, and SQL files to identify insecure) Tj
T*
(patterns such as unsanitised input, outdated cryptography, and missing authorisation) Tj
T*
(checks.) Tj
T*
(2. **Dependency and configuration audit:** Reviewed configuration files and database) Tj
T*
(schema to uncover hard-coded secrets and weak defaults.) Tj
T*
(3. **Manual functional testing:** Exercised login, registration, booking, and) Tj
T*
(administrative workflows in a local environment to validate exploitability and) Tj
T*
(confirm fixes.) Tj
T*
(4. **Automated linting:** Executed `php -l` against modified files to ensure syntax) Tj
T*
(correctness and reduce regression risk.) Tj
T*
(5. **Threat modelling:** Mapped attack surfaces \(public forms, file uploads,) Tj
T*
(administrative actions, OAuth callbacks\) to prioritise remediation effort.) Tj
T*
T*
(3. Vulnerability Summary) Tj
T*
(# | Vulnerability | Location | Risk | Status) Tj
T*
T*
(--- | --------------- | ---------- | ------ | --------) Tj
T*
T*
(1 | Hard-coded root database credentials and lack of connection error handling |) Tj
T*
(`inc/connection.inc.php`, `admin/includes/connection.inc.php` | High | Fixed) Tj
T*
(2 | Session cookies missing secure attributes, enabling session hijacking | Global) Tj
