T*
(4.4 Weak password hashing) Tj
T*
(• **Original issue:** User passwords were hashed with `md5\(\)` during registration) Tj
T*
(and compared with MD5 digests on login. MD5 is collision-prone and GPU-crackable) Tj
T*
(within seconds.) Tj
T*
(• **Impact:** A database leak would immediately expose all user passwords, enabling) Tj
T*
(credential stuffing.) Tj
T*
(• **Fix:** Migrated to PHP's `password_hash\(\)`/`password_verify\(\)` APIs with the) Tj
T*
(default bcrypt algorithm, regenerated password hashes for default accounts, and) Tj
T*
(updated the schema to accommodate stronger hashes.) Tj
T*
T*
(4.5 Stored cross-site scripting \(XSS\)) Tj
T*
(• **Original issue:** User-supplied values such as booking messages, vehicle titles,) Tj
T*
(and other metadata were stored unfiltered and echoed directly into HTML contexts) Tj
T*
(throughout the site \(customer dashboards and admin panels\).) Tj
T*
(• **Impact:** Authenticated attackers could inject JavaScript that executes in other) Tj
T*
(users' browsers, leading to session theft or administrative compromise.) Tj
T*
(• **Fix:** Introduced sanitisation helpers for inbound data, escaped all dynamic) Tj
T*
(output with `htmlspecialchars\(\)`, and audited templates to ensure untrusted values) Tj
T*
(are never rendered raw.) Tj
T*
T*
(4.6 Cross-site request forgery \(CSRF\)) Tj
T*
(• **Original issue:** High-impact state-changing forms \(login, registration,) Tj
T*
(bookings, admin approvals, vehicle uploads\) lacked CSRF tokens. Browsers would) Tj
T*
(happily submit forged requests triggered from malicious sites.) Tj
T*
(• **Impact:** Attackers could trick authenticated users into confirming bookings,) Tj
T*
(adding vehicles, or changing account data without consent.) Tj
T*
(• **Fix:** Implemented reusable CSRF helpers \(`generate_csrf_token`,) Tj
T*
(`require_valid_csrf_token`\) and embedded hidden tokens in every sensitive form.) Tj
T*
(Server-side handlers now reject requests with missing or invalid tokens.) Tj
T*
T*
(4.7 Arbitrary file upload) Tj
T*
(• **Original issue:** The admin vehicle upload feature accepted any file name and) Tj
T*
(extension, storing it directly under the public `img/vehicleimages/` directory) Tj
T*
(without validation or randomisation.) Tj
T*
(• **Impact:** An attacker with admin access could upload a PHP web shell and achieve) Tj
T*
(remote code execution. Even non-admin attackers could exploit stolen admin sessions) Tj
T*
(\(see CSRF issue\) to plant malware.) Tj
T*
(• **Fix:** Restricted uploads to approved MIME types, generated randomised) Tj
T*
(filenames, stored metadata safely, and verified move operations before persisting) Tj
T*
(references.) Tj
T*
T*
(5. OAuth / OpenID Connect Integration) Tj
T*
(A new Google OpenID Connect login flow was added to support social sign-on. The) Tj
T*
(implementation:) Tj
T*
ET
